WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
Switch on an ordinary lamp.

2
00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:06.480
Its light leaves in random
directions, with random phases.

3
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.380
Laser light is different.

4
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:12.010
It leaves as a narrow beam,
at a single frequency.

5
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.490
And it is coherent: every crest lined up,

6
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.800
the waves marching in step.

7
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.540
How can a crowd of atoms be made
to send out light in perfect step?

8
00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:26.190
In this mission, you'll find out
what a population inversion is,

9
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.510
and why a laser can't
amplify light without one.

10
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:34.220
Then you'll look inside a laser: a
pumped medium between two mirrors,

11
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.260
one of them letting light out.

12
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:41.560
Your mission: explain how a laser makes
its light waves march in perfect step.
